; Leaf library: no library dependencies at all.
;
; `Cow_table` is the copy-on-write sharded map that most of the engine's read-mostly
; caches are built on. It lives here, rather than in `concurrency`, because two
; lower-level libraries need it and both sit *below* `concurrency` in the dependency
; graph — `logging` (which everything, including `concurrency`, depends on) and
; `latency_profiling`. Putting it in `concurrency` would have made their use of it a
; dependency cycle, and duplicating the implementation in each would leave three copies
; of the trickiest code in the repo.
;
; Keep this library dependency-free. It is the bottom of the graph.
(library
 (name ds)
 (public_name dio.data_structures)
 ; the wrapped alias module is `Ds`, so call sites read `Ds.Cow_table`
 (modules Cow_table))
